Guard the legacy main-screen plugin calls behind DISABLE_DEPRECATED.

EditorMainScreen::add_main_plugin() and ::remove_main_plugin() are declared and
defined only inside #ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED (editor/editor_main_screen.h,
editor/editor_main_screen.cpp) -- they are the legacy path that wraps a plugin's
main screen into an EditorDock via LegacyMainScreenContainer.  Their two call
sites in EditorNode::add_editor_plugin()/remove_editor_plugin(), however, carry
no guard at all, so building with deprecated=no (which the ebuild passes when
USE=-deprecated, defining -DDISABLE_DEPRECATED) fails with:

    editor/editor_node.cpp:4450:48: error: 'class EditorMainScreen' has no
        member named 'add_main_plugin'
    editor/editor_node.cpp:4461:48: error: 'class EditorMainScreen' has no
        member named 'remove_main_plugin'

EditorPlugin::has_main_screen() itself is declared outside the guard
(editor/plugins/editor_plugin.h), so only the two calls need covering; a grep
over the tree confirms editor_node.cpp holds the only uses outside
editor_main_screen.{h,cpp}.

The whole `if` is wrapped rather than just its body: with the body gone the
condition would be a pure no-op, and has_main_screen() may dispatch into
GDVIRTUAL0RC(bool, _has_main_screen) on script/extension plugins, i.e. run
user code for a result nothing consumes.

Not an upstream mirror: master still carries the unguarded calls at the same
lines and no issue or PR covers it, so this stays until upstream either guards

